  "body": "## Overview\nThis PR completes Phase 1 and 2 of the colossal Rockbox DSP restoration project, setting up the complete dual-backend architecture and UI navigation for all 10+ advanced DSP processors while preserving the working external/Spotify audio session linkage.\n\n## Architecture / Dual-Backend\n- Created `AudioProcessingBackend` interface to abstract the engine away from direct Android APIs.\n- Migrated existing working external connection logic into `ExternalSessionAudioBackend`.\n- Scaffolded `PcmDspBackend` which will house the actual ExoPlayer/AudioTrack biquad, timestretch, and crossfeed math.\n- Introduced `DspCapability` mapping so modules correctly state `UNSUPPORTED_EXTERNAL_SESSION` instead of lying when using Spotify.\n\n## 10-Band EQ & Mapping\n- Updated `AudioEngine` to track a full virtual 10-band Rockbox parametric EQ.\n- Added interpolation mapping in `ExternalSessionAudioBackend` to project the 10 virtual bands onto the detected N native `Equalizer` bands provided by the device vendor.\n\n## UI Restoration\n- Refactored `WaveForgeApp` Bottom Navigation to expose the major required sections: Dashboard, EQ, DSP Hub, Playback, and Settings.\n- Created nested Compose screens (`SpatialScreen`, `DynamicsScreen`, `EnhancementScreen`, `ProcessingScreen`, `PlaybackScreen`) exposing all the Rockbox modules (Haas Surround, Crossfeed, PBE, AFR, Compressor, Limiter).\n- Expanded `SettingsScreen` diagnostics to dump capability matrices for every processor.\n\n## Testing\n- Preserved existing external-audio hook. App builds and dynamically detects Spotify.\n- `UNSUPPORTED_EXTERNAL_SESSION` displays truthfully on advanced modules when attached to Spotify, adhering to the NO FAKE DSP rule.",
